# Web3Forms access key for the application form (src/components/sections/ApplyForm.tsx).
#
# Get one at https://web3forms.com - it is tied to the destination email address.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ is required: the site is a static export, so this is inlined into
# the client bundle at build time. Web3Forms access keys are designed to be
# public; they identify an inbox and grant no account access.
#
# The real value lives in .env.local (gitignored). For deploys that build in CI
# (Cloudflare Pages), set it in the build environment too - .env.local is not
# committed, so a CI build without it ships a form that cannot submit.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=

# hCaptcha site key for the application form. Optional.
#
# Defaults in code to the sitekey Web3Forms publishes for free-plan accounts,
# so leave this blank unless you are on a paid plan with your own key. It is
# public either way - hCaptcha reads it out of the markup.
#
# hCaptcha must ALSO be enabled for this form in the Web3Forms dashboard.
# Without that, Web3Forms accepts submissions that carry no token and the
# widget protects nothing.
NEXT_PUBLIC_HCAPTCHA_SITEKEY=
